  "body": "#2337: the user guide does not describe the progress overlay of #2274.\n\n**Stacked on #2274.** This branch starts at the head of #2274 (43b789ed). Thus the diff against `main` also shows the commits of #2274. Review only the last commit, 4cc0d7bf. Merge this PR after #2274.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `site/content/guide/operations/_index.md`, section \"Generating\": two new paragraphs. They tell the user these items:\n  - In the desktop app, a toolpath generates in the background.\n  - The panel at the top centre of the viewport shows the operation name, \"(2 of 5)\" when more operations wait, the elapsed seconds, an activity bar and **Cancel generation**.\n  - The panel goes away when the toolpath lands, when generation is refused (the message stays in the status line), or on Cancel.\n  - Cancel keeps the old toolpath and drops the waiting operations.\n  - The window stays usable. An edit, undo or delete of the operation during generation discards the result, and the status line asks for a new generation.\n  - **Regenerate all stale** still runs in one step, without the panel.\n- Each statement comes from the code of #2274 (`crates/ui/src/gen_worker.rs`, `crates/ui/src/egui_app/gen_overlay.rs`). The button names match the UI strings: `Cancel generation` (`gen_overlay::CANCEL`) and `Regenerate all stale` (`panes.rs`).\n- Text only. No screenshot is committed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- `site/tests/test_guide_navigation.py` was not run: Python is not installed on this machine. The change adds no link, heading or front matter.\n- The site was not built.\n\nChangelog: none (docs only)\n\nFixes #2337\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
